1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,337
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:09,009
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,227
[in English] …is a master of disguise.

7
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:21,229
[in English] Do you know this man?

8
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:22,897
- [Audrey, in English] No.
- [cell phone clatters]

9
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:24,691
[Dmitri, in English]
<i>I can help you find this man.</i>

10
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:27,485
[in English] I know
a very good tracker, a man hunter.

11
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:28,570
[Samir, in English] <i>Hello, Ambassador.</i>

12
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:31,573
[in English] I think
we need the help of Mr. Dmitri.

13
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,034
Our target is Boss KM.

14
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,786
[Emerson] <i>And the suitcase</i>
<i>with five million pesos.</i>

15
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:37,871
What is this?

16
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:38,913
[Emerson] <i>You'll wear that,</i>

17
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:42,500
<i>because that's the uniform</i>
<i>of Atoy's new breakout group.</i>

18
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:45,837
I'm the OG child of Tatoy's thread.

19
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,422
[Audrey] <i>Where is Ibyang?</i>

20
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:50,383
Her real mother took her.

21
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,384
[Audrey] <i>Who is she?</i>

22
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:52,844
Why did she only show up now?

23
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,220
[in English] Good morning!

24
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:57,307
Come to my set. I need an extra actress.

25
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,391
Where is that?

26
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,101
Can I come with you?

27
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,103
No, you can't! Stay here!

28
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,314
[Charmi] <i>You left her? Alone?</i>

29
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:06,941
I won't miss my chance to be famous.

30
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:07,942
Feeling main character!

31
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:09,360
[goon actor 1] <i>I'll riddle her</i>
<i>with bullets.</i>

32
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:10,653
<i>I'll use them all on her!</i>

33
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:11,863
[Ibyang] <i>Kill Mama?</i>

34
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:13,656
- [in English] Action!
- [grunting]

35
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,492
[screaming and panicking]

36
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:18,036
PREVIOUSLY

37
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:22,582
Run now! Run!

38
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:24,876
[screaming and panicking]

39
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,127
Mama!

40
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,671
[objects clanging]

41
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,799
- [gasping]
- [squeals]

42
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:32,050
[objects clattering]

43
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:33,134
[in English] Cut!

44
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:35,136
[director] What's happening here?!

45
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,346
Get out of there!

46
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,556
[director] You're disturbing my set!
Who are you?!

47
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,933
You broke the equipment!

48
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,142
I'm sorry.

49
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,560
I didn't mean to!

50
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,729
"Sorry"?! Wait. Who are you?!

51
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,648
Hey, Al! Who is this?

52
00:01:46,731 --> 00:01:48,233
- Whose child is this?!
- I don't know, Director.

53
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,275
- She just came in.
- What do you mean you don't know?!

54
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,360
You should know!

55
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:51,736
Hey. Who are you?

56
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,238
She's my mom.

57
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:54,531
[director] Huh?

58
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:56,616
- Olga?!
- [Olga] Director.

59
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:59,119
This is your child?
Why did you bring her to the filming?

60
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,829
Look what happened!

61
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,914
Director, I'm sorry.

62
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:05,041
She's just a child.

63
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:06,584
I'll take care of it!

64
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,253
Oh, so you'll take care of it!

65
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,756
The broken equipment
will be deducted from my budget!

66
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,258
[shrieks] You're driving me crazy!

67
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:14,968
And your dream, huh.

68
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,177
Your dream of fame?

69
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,804
Forget it.

70
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:19,222
Al, fix this!

71
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:20,557
[director] Back to one!

72
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,183
This is insane!

73
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:23,476
[somber music playing]

74
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,186
[director] Fix it, Al!

75
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:29,649
[music fades]

76
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:31,901
[suave theme music playing]

77
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:59,762
[music fades]

78
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:02,807
- [Karla] Brother Kurt.
- Oh?

79
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:04,142
Where's your costume?

80
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:06,019
- Oh, it's inside. Yes.
- Ah.

81
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:07,312
Here it is.

82
00:03:07,395 --> 00:03:09,022
- Boss.
- Isn't Ame here yet?

83
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:10,732
- It's already nine o'clock!
- Looks like she's not coming.

84
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:12,817
We can't be late.

85
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,403
[phone ringing]

86
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:17,906
We should leave now. We might be late.

87
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,908
Hello? Where are you?

88
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,659
Look to your right.

89
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:25,038
[light music playing]

90
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:26,080
Are you leaving now?

91
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:28,625
Yes, we're just waiting for Sister Ame.

92
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:30,543
Remember what we talked about, okay?

93
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:34,255
Just follow our car. Okay?

94
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:36,591
[in English] Oh! okay. Copy, copy.

95
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:39,010
[Emerson] Psst, Karla.

96
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,762
Who are you talking to?

97
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:42,263
[Karla] No one, uh…

98
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,806
It's just T-Bak. She's pestering me.

99
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,225
You know.

100
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:47,060
[in English] T-Bak, okay.

101
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:48,061
Yes.

102
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,520
You're sure, huh.

103
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:52,857
- Oh, Ame's here.
- Hey!

104
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:54,317
[Karla] Oh, there she is.
She brought so much.

105
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,236
- [Emerson] Thank God you're finally here.
- Sorry!

106
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:57,195
- [in English] Thank you, Lord.
- [in English] Thank you.

107
00:03:57,278 --> 00:04:01,157
I had to clean the shop, then Audrey came.

108
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:03,243
We chatted about Olga.

109
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,870
- Where's your uniform?
- Yes.

110
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,914
- Oh. I forgot.
- [Kurt] Yes.

111
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:09,624
That's what I'm afraid of.

112
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:11,084
Just get it later. Come on, it's late.

113
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,460
Oh! [chuckles]

114
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,836
Nice!

115
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,839
You're all wearing suspenders.

116
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:18,174
Are you going to dance?

117
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:20,343
- Oh, no, no.
- We could.

118
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:21,761
Well… Uh…

119
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:23,304
We're going on a field trip.

120
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:25,098
- Ah, field trip! Where?
- [Karla] Yes.

121
00:04:25,181 --> 00:04:26,849
[stammering] To-- Uh, uh--

122
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,351
Ah, Miss Siony.

123
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:30,812
Don't you ever take a day off
from gossiping?

124
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:32,605
Even vehicles have number coding,

125
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:33,898
so they stop plying the streets.

126
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,693
You know, I'm just curious and concerned.

127
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:39,279
What if you don't come back
from that field trip?

128
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,238
Oh. That's exaggerated.

129
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:44,534
At least, someone knows
where to find you, and that's me.

130
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:45,535
That's too much.

131
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:46,703
"Won't be able to come back."

132
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,080
Miss Siony, thanks for the concern.

133
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:50,456
But we're not going to war.

134
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:53,001
- It's just a field trip.
- [Karla] Yes.

135
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,461
We're just going nearby.
We'll come back, promise.

136
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,630
- That's true.
- [Emerson] Okay then. Bye!

137
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,299
- Bye! We're leaving, Miss Siony!
- [overlapping chatter]

138
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:00,550
Okay, okay. We'll go ahead.

139
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:01,884
[Siony] Snacks. Don't you want some?!

140
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:04,053
- [Emerson] We're good. Bye!
- [Siony] Chips!

141
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,221
[Emerson] Bye, Miss Siony!

142
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:07,015
[Siony] Food for your trip.

143
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:09,934
[music fades]

144
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:32,582
[chuckles softly]

145
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:33,708
Hey.

146
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,752
Good thing you could come.

147
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,379
Brother Kurt couldn't come.
He had an emergency,

148
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:40,214
so we dropped him off
on the highway earlier.

149
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,216
I'm game for anything.
As long as I can help.

150
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,427
Wait. What's our group's name?

151
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:46,804
Child of the tailor?

152
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:48,014
Child of the tailor.

153
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:49,682
- Child of the thread!
- [Paldo] Oh?

154
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,894
That's minus points for the title.

155
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,270
Oh, make up for it!

156
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:55,521
[Paldo] Oh, sorry! My bad.

157
00:05:55,605 --> 00:06:00,318
Wait. Does Atoy know I'm here?

158
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:03,362
I really want to make amends
for the mistakes I made against him.

159
00:06:04,363 --> 00:06:05,907
I already convinced him.

160
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,992
I told him you're the replacement for now.

161
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,368
- So, you better make it up to me.
- [Paldo] Oh, there you go.

162
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:12,163
- You're something else, Emerson!
- Yes.

163
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:13,581
[Emerson] Okay, then.

164
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,249
No one gets off yet.

165
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,835
- I'll go first, just to observe.
- Okay, okay.

166
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,087
Wait for me.

167
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:22,507
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

168
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,601
[music fades]

169
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:43,486
[suspicious music playing]

170
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:53,079
Oh.

171
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:54,497
Oh, Brother Emerso…

172
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,998
You're here too?

173
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,041
Yes.

174
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,001
What are you doing here?

175
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:00,920
Uh, uh…

176
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:02,839
Cathy and I have a date.

177
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:05,591
There's a famous restaurant there.
We'll eat there.

178
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:08,845
Date with Cathy.

179
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:11,013
[sneaky music playing]

180
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,473
Why are your nostrils flaring?

181
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:13,766
Looks like you're lying.

182
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,518
No!

183
00:07:15,601 --> 00:07:18,020
Your father sent you here,
didn't he, to spy on us?

184
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,272
No! No!

185
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:21,107
It's not like that, promise.

186
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:24,277
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

187
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,612
Don't mess with me, Gavin.

188
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:27,989
Don't mess with me.

189
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:30,324
[in English] Fine.

190
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:34,245
I followed you
because I found out you had a mission.

191
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:35,997
[in English] I just want to help you guys.

192
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:40,543
How did you know that?
Who told you? Karla?

193
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:42,545
Ah. No, no. No, sir, no.

194
00:07:43,087 --> 00:07:44,839
I just overheard you talking.

195
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,090
[in English] Don't worry!

196
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,341
[in English] Your secret is safe with me.

197
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:49,010
[in English] I'm not here to sabotage you.

198
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:50,970
I also won't tell Dad, promise.

199
00:07:51,053 --> 00:07:53,014
[in English] I just really
want to help you guys.

200
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:55,725
I promise, I promise.

201
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:57,477
I'm just here to help.

202
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,146
[suspicious music playing]

203
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,691
[music fades]

204
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:05,193
[Emerson] There, okay.

205
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:06,652
Let's check if it's all good.

206
00:08:08,237 --> 00:08:10,781
- Thread 1, Thread 2.
- [Karla, in English] Copy.

207
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:12,200
Thread 3?

208
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,659
[in English] Loud and clear.

209
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:14,744
Thread 4?

210
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:16,871
[in English] Loud and clear.

211
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:18,122
[in English] Okay.

212
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,332
[suspicious music playing]

213
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:20,958
[in English] Target number 1.

214
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:23,294
Needle.

215
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:25,588
Kevin Martinez. He's the mastermind.

216
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:29,842
Target number 2. Scissors.

217
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:33,387
[Emerson] That's Boyet, the courier.

218
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,934
And the suitcase of money…

219
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,393
- [both] Buttons!
- [in English] Okay.

220
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,855
[phone rings]

221
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:47,068
[in English] Hello, Atoy?

222
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,236
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

223
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:50,029
Good morning, children of the thread.

224
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,197
[in English] Is everything in place?

225
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:53,115
- [both, in English] Yes, Master!
- [in English] Yes, Master.

226
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:55,952
Ah, Ame is with us.

227
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:58,955
And Paldo is here, replacing Brother Kurt.

228
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,707
We can handle this, Atoy.

229
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,251
[Atoy on the phone, in English] <i>Very good.</i>

230
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:05,253
<i>I trust your abilities, but…</i>

231
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:07,296
[in English] I just
have one last reminder.

232
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:10,299
[Atoy on the phone] <i>No mission</i>
<i>is more important than your lives.</i>

233
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:12,552
If you know it's dangerous,

234
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,804
abort immediately. Copy?

235
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:16,180
[all, in English] Yes, Master!

236
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,181
[in English] Good.

237
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,599
Make sure you don't get caught,

238
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:21,394
and most important of all, no one dies.

239
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:22,937
- [both, in English] Yes, Master!
- [in English] Yes, Master.

240
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,065
Atoy, thank you.

241
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:28,109
Thanks for letting me join.

242
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:29,569
Don't worry.

243
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,696
I won't fail them.

244
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:32,655
[in English] Good luck.

245
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:38,244
Uh, wait.

246
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:40,913
We have one more companion

247
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,957
that Atoy shouldn't know about.

248
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:44,709
Who?

249
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:48,838
- [in English] Hi, guys.
- Gavin?!

250
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,549
What are you doing here?

251
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:54,510
Brother caught me, so…

252
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,095
he allowed me to join.

253
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:58,139
What will your role be?

254
00:09:58,222 --> 00:09:59,390
Mm-hmm.

255
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:02,018
He'll be the lookout
outside the function room.

256
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:04,604
He wasn't part of the original plan.

257
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,230
Oh, that's fine, whatever.

258
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:08,316
As long as I'm part of your adventure.

259
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,444
[in English] Okay. Ready?

260
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:14,739
[in English] Okay.

261
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:16,907
[in English] One, two, three…

262
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:18,034
- [all, in English] Let's go!
- [in English] Go!

263
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:19,201
What? What?

264
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:20,119
- What's that?
- I thought…

265
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:21,162
That's not <i>Maalis, Taya</i>!

266
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:22,455
What are you doing? Don't…

267
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,706
We're already wrong. We're just starting.

268
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:25,916
We'll stick together! Okay?

269
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,877
[in English] One, two, three…

270
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,629
- [all] You're it!
- Huh?

271
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,464
- Brother, what's that?
- Where did you get that?

272
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:33,466
What-- Let's just say "game".
Can we say "game" instead?

273
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:35,301
- [Karla] Okay!
- [in English] Game, okay?

274
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:37,345
One… Game, okay! Say "game", okay.

275
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,429
- [all] Game, game, game!
- [in English] Okay.

276
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:39,722
[in English] One, two, three.

277
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:41,057
[all, in English] Game!

278
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,683
[upbeat rock music playing]

279
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,143
Here are your badges,

280
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,811
clothes, and sandals.

281
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,814
[manager] Return them
after the event, okay?

282
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:49,774
[in English] Yes, ma'am.

283
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,734
[in English] Also, no heavy makeup.

284
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:53,194
Just glass skin.

285
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:56,572
Natural, but goddess-like look.

286
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,408
And once we start,

287
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:01,619
you'll welcome the guests.

288
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:03,829
[in English] Assist them to their seats.

289
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,665
And when the bid is awarded,

290
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:10,086
you'll approach the winning bidder
to have them sign the form.

291
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:11,295
Got it?

292
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:12,296
[all, in English] Yes, ma'am.

293
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:16,384
[in English] Also, you have to communicate
with them in English.

294
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,761
The bidders here are high-class.

295
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,679
[manager] You know that, right?

296
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,515
With all their money,

297
00:11:22,598 --> 00:11:24,975
they don't even know where to spend it.

298
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:26,227
I wish I were like that.

299
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,020
[in English] Anyway, any questions?

300
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:30,272
[in English] We better get moving.
Come on.

301
00:11:30,356 --> 00:11:33,359
[mid-tempo action music playing]

302
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:48,040
[music fades]

303
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:56,132
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

304
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:57,716
[whistling]

305
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:58,968
[in English] Oh, sorry.

306
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:05,307
I'll take this.

307
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:12,064
[giggles]

308
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,900
Okay. Right?

309
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:16,318
[in English] As always.

310
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:20,281
You're the best, Emerson!

311
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,283
So good, right?

312
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,328
[clears throat]

313
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:31,125
[whistling]

314
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:41,010
[suspicious music playing]

315
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:54,148
Thanks for doing my face.
I really don't know how to do makeup.

316
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:56,484
No worries, sis. You look beautiful.

317
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:05,451
[suspicious music playing]

318
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:09,830
[in English] Hi!

319
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:11,790
[in English] Mr. Alferez, please.

320
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:14,668
All right, um, kindly fill this out.

321
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,378
[in English] Sure.

322
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:23,344
- [in English] Number.
- [in English] Thank you.

323
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,472
- [in English] Mr. Alferez.
- [Alfarez, in English] Hi.

324
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:27,473
[in English] Let me
take you to your table.

325
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:28,557
[in English] Sure.

326
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:36,440
[suspicious music playing]

327
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,489
[in English] Thread 2, this is Thread 1.

328
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:44,949
I've arrived here too. Over.

329
00:13:51,121 --> 00:13:52,456
[in English] This way, sir.

330
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:02,007
[in English] Thread 3, update on ETA.

331
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:03,926
[in English] This is Thread 3.

332
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:05,177
[in English] ETA unknown.

333
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,137
Huh? Why?

334
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:10,641
Mini Thread 4 had a wardrobe malfunction.

335
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:14,270
[Paldo on the device] <i>But we're fixing it.</i>

336
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,189
Hurry up. We need you here.

337
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,274
[in English] Okay, okay.

338
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:19,692
Uh, is it tight?

339
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:21,193
Here, attach the other side.

340
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,361
[music fades]

341
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:26,949
[tense music playing]

342
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,326
- [in English] Hello.
- [in English] Yes.

343
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:31,620
[in English] Sorry.

344
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,632
The needle is here.

345
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:45,843
I repeat, the needle is here.

346
00:14:46,468 --> 00:14:47,928
- [in English] Sir Kevin Martinez!
- [in English] Yes?

347
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,388
[in English] Let me
take you to your table.

348
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:50,639
[Kevin, in English] Thank you.

349
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:52,558
[in English] This way, sir.

350
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,687
[music fades]

351
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,231
[tense music playing]

352
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:00,399
[in English] This way, sir.

353
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:25,382
[in English] Sir, wine.

354
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,217
[in English] Thank you.

355
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:35,142
[upbeat rock music playing]

356
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,239
[usherette] Mr. Meneses.

357
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:53,994
That's me.

358
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:08,509
[music fades]

359
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,552
[in English] Hello, sir.
I'll take you to your seat.

360
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:12,596
[in English] This way.

361
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:18,477
[suspicious music playing]

362
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:31,323
[tense music playing]

363
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:41,125
[in English] Wine, sir, ma'am.

364
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:48,424
[music swells]

365
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,592
[music fades]

366
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,594
[intense music playing]

367
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:53,721
Good afternoon,

368
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,681
Ma'am Odette, Ma'am Malou.

369
00:17:03,605 --> 00:17:05,315
[in English] Hello, Cathy!

370
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:08,235
[Cathy on the phone, in English]
<i>Uh, babe, where are you?</i>

371
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:11,155
Can we meet?

372
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:13,240
Ah, uh…

373
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,659
[Cathy on the phone, in English]
<i>I'll be free in a few minutes.</i>

374
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,911
I just accompanied Mommy to an event.

375
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:19,872
[suspicious music playing]

376
00:17:19,955 --> 00:17:22,416
Sorry, I already have plans.

377
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:24,835
I went with Jason to Batangas.

378
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:27,421
[in English] I think
he's going to visit someone.

379
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,715
[in English] Oh, um…

380
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:33,218
Okay. Let's just talk tomorrow?

381
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,596
[in English] Yes, yes. Sure.

382
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:37,556
[in English] Okay, bye.

383
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,230
[muffled chattering]

384
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:47,775
[Cathy] All right.

385
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:51,487
[music swells]

386
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,824
[host, in English] Good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

387
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:58,994
[in English] Welcome
to Palladium Auction House.

388
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:03,999
[in English] Tonight,
we have very exciting art pieces

389
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,459
for you to bid on.

390
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:07,252
[in English] Starting with…

391
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,633
<i>With My Child's Hands.</i>

392
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,929
[in English] Painted by Alexis Florence.

393
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,223
[in English] The starting bid

394
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:23,393
will be 100,000 pesos.

395
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,396
[in English] Do I hear 150?

396
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,981
[suspicious music playing]

397
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:32,069
[in English] One-fifty, from number 17.

398
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,695
[in English] Two hundred!

399
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:38,867
[in English] Two hundred,
from the lady, number 22.

400
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:41,120
[in English] Three hundred.

401
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:46,083
Three hundred, again
from the gentleman, number 17.

402
00:18:46,583 --> 00:18:47,876
[in English] Five hundred thousand!

403
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,630
[in English] Five hundred thousand pesos!

404
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:55,676
[in English] From the gentleman
of number 27.

405
00:18:56,635 --> 00:18:59,763
[applauding]

406
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,266
Five hundred thousand for that?

407
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,434
Ibyang's drawing is even better.

408
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:07,354
Leave it alone. This is really
just a money-throwing event.

409
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:09,648
[Karla over device] <i>I just hope</i>
<i>the money they're using</i>

410
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:13,277
were obtained through clean means.

411
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:16,572
[in English] Do I hear 550?

412
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,118
[in English] Nothing?

413
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:25,581
[in English] Going once,

414
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:27,916
going twice.

415
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,962
[in English] Sold to the gentleman
of number 27.

416
00:19:32,045 --> 00:19:35,549
[in English] Mr. Alferez, I believe.

417
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:37,092
[in English] Thank you so much.

418
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:41,221
[applauding]

419
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:42,973
[in English] Sir, please sign this.

420
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:56,528
- [melancholic music playing]
- [phone ringing]

421
00:20:00,115 --> 00:20:01,366
[Atoy on the phone] <i>Oh, Ibyang?</i>

422
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:03,243
<i>I'm on my way to work.</i>

423
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:04,745
That's why I called you.

424
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,497
[Atoy on the phone] <i>And yes, I miss you.</i>

425
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:10,000
Ibyang?

426
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,129
Ibyang.

427
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:16,840
Are you there?

428
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:20,969
I broke something at Mama's work.

429
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:24,806
[sobbing]

430
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:28,227
She got scolded because of me.

431
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:31,396
[ibyang sobbing]

432
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:36,068
Maybe Mama doesn't want me
to be her child anymore.

433
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:37,945
[sobbing]

434
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:38,946
[scoffs]

435
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:41,949
What are you saying, Ibyang?
Don't say that.

436
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:45,077
If you made a mistake, then apologize.

437
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:49,289
But most important of all, make up for it.

438
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:51,750
How?

439
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:53,126
[Atoy on the phone] <i>Simple.</i>

440
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,212
Be good.

441
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:56,880
Then tell her,

442
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,799
"I won't do it again."

443
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:00,008
Right?

444
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:04,388
Ibyang, your mother
searched for you for so long.

445
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:07,474
Right? I'm sure she loves you very much.

446
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:08,976
She'll understand you.

447
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:14,064
But she's not talking to me.

448
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:15,232
[sobs]

449
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:18,652
Maybe she'll leave me again.

450
00:21:18,735 --> 00:21:20,737
Ibyang, Ibyang,

451
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:23,532
no parent would do that to their child

452
00:21:23,615 --> 00:21:25,284
just because of one mistake.

453
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:28,328
I'm sure she loves you.

454
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,747
I just wish

455
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:34,751
you were here with me.

456
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:37,296
But we're here.

457
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:39,464
We're just here, okay.

458
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,718
You're with us, and I'll never leave you.

459
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:43,969
Remember that.

460
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:49,099
[melodramatic music playing]

461
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:58,358
[Audrey on the phone, in English]
<i>Dad, I'll be a little late.</i>

462
00:21:58,442 --> 00:21:59,318
[in English] <i>It's traffic.</i>

463
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:00,485
[in English] Don't worry, dear.

464
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,404
The people I'm meeting with
aren't here yet.

465
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,197
[in English] I'll see you in a while.

466
00:22:05,365 --> 00:22:06,533
[in English] Bye-bye.

467
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:10,245
[muffled chattering in the distance]

468
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,248
[somber music playing]

469
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:14,499
[Dmitri, in English] Gentlemen!

470
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,044
[in English] Have your seat.

471
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:18,170
[in English] Thank you.

472
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:24,217
[in English] To what
do I owe this pleasure?

473
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:26,636
[in Russian/English] Good day, Mr. Dmitri!

474
00:22:27,429 --> 00:22:29,639
[in English] We spoke
with Ambassador Petrov.

475
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:32,851
[in English] And he said
maybe you can help us.

476
00:22:34,561 --> 00:22:36,480
[in English] Do you have a tracker?

477
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:39,232
[pensive music playing]

478
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:40,901
[in English] Yes.

479
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:42,652
[in English] Is he good?

480
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:45,989
[in English] Yes, very.

481
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:50,202
[in English] Is there something or someone
you need to find?

482
00:22:50,952 --> 00:22:52,829
[security officer, in English]
This man, Mr. Regalia.

483
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:56,917
[in English] He broke into our embassy
and stole from us.

484
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:57,876
[clears throat]

485
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,629
[in English] Is there
something wrong, Mr. Regalia?

486
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:05,383
[rousing music playing]

487
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:15,685
[electronic blipping]

488
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:21,441
[tense music playing]

489
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:23,276
[Audrey, in English] <i>I think</i>
<i>you've got the wrong idea.</i>

490
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:25,987
[in English] What is the matter?
You have another lover?

491
00:23:26,071 --> 00:23:27,489
[in English] Maybe he's good in bed.

492
00:23:27,572 --> 00:23:29,032
[in English] You give me a try.

493
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:30,700
[in Russian] You're vulgar!

494
00:23:30,784 --> 00:23:32,953
Thread 1 is compromised. Help.

495
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:34,246
[Paldo, in English] <i>This is Thread 3.</i>

496
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,748
[Paldo] <i>I'll take care of the needle.</i>

497
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:41,086
[Mercado on the device, in English]
<i>The laptop is locked</i>

498
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:42,129
<i>and requires a code.</i>

499
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:43,380
<i>Aside from the ambassador,</i>

500
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:46,049
<i>the only person who knows the code</i>

501
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,677
<i>is the head of IT at the embassy,</i>

502
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,303
<i>Lily Santiago.</i>

503
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,264
UP NEXT

504
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:53,682
Son of a thread.

505
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:57,185
[gunshots]

506
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,061
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

507
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:00,438
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

508
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:03,567
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

509
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:05,944
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

510
00:24:06,027 --> 00:24:07,237
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
